'''Nabat''' was a [[city]] inhabited by [[Twi'lek]]s on their home [[planet]] [[Ryloth]]. Around [[21 BBY]], during the [[Battle of Ryloth]], the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]' [[Separatist Droid Army|droid army]] seized control of the city and took its inhabitants hostage. After its capture, the Twi'leks were used by the Confederacy as living shields to prevent a direct assault from the [[Galactic Republic]] on their [[J-1 proton cannon]]s. However, despite the Confederacy's efforts, Nabat was later liberated by [[Jedi General]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and his [[clone trooper]]s from [[Ghost Company]], which allowed the Republic to continue their mission to free Ryloth from the Confederacy.

==Description==
Located on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Ryloth]], the [[city]] of Nabat was constructed within a rocky area of large [[forest]]. Many of its structures were built from rock, with multiple stretching one or two stories in height. Nabat's also possessed outer walls of stone and a large courtyard with a circular space in the center.<ref name="Innocents" />

==History==
{{Quote|We need to remember why we're here. We came to aid the Twi'leks, not destroy their home. Cody?''"<br />"''That means we'll be taking it back the hard way. Minimal destruction with blasters and droid poppers only. No rockets or detonators. Check your aim. Keep an eye out for the locals.|Obi-Wan and Cody prepare the men for the battle|<ref name="Innocents" />}}
During the [[Clone Wars]], Nabat was [[Battle of Ryloth|conquered and occupied]] by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Confederacy's]] [[Separatist Droid Army|Droid Army]]<ref name="Storm Over Ryloth">{{TCW|Storm Over Ryloth}}</ref> under [[TX-20]]. There, TX-20 set up a battery of five [[J-1 proton cannon]]s in the main square.<ref name="Innocents" />

[[File:Ghost_Company2.png|thumb|left|275px|Ghost Company scouts out Nabat]]
When the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] attacked, [[Emir]] [[Wat Tambor|Tambor]] ordered TX-20 not to allow them to land on the surface. Anticipating this, TX-20 rounded up all of Nabat's survivors, except [[Numa]], and used them as a living shield, preventing Republic forces from firing at their artillery. [[Jedi General]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and the [[clone trooper]]s of [[Ghost Company]] attempted to land despite the heavy artillery, taking six [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry]] gunships down to the surface and landing in the forests outside the city, arming themselves only with [[blaster rifle]]s and [[electromagnetic pulse grenade]]s so as to not cause damage to the locals or the town itself. Due to the artillery, [[Jedi]] [[General]] [[Mace Windu]] and his [[Acclamator-class transgalactic military assault ship|transport ships]] could not land safely, leaving Ghost Company on their own to take Nabat. Only a few of the gunships made it through the artillery barrage and landed troops.<ref name="Innocents" />

After the troops fought past Separatist [[battle droid]]s on the outside of the city walls, they entered Nabat only to learn that it was deserted. General Kenobi sent scouts ahead, with troopers "[[Boil]]" and "[[Waxer]]" heading to the south sector of the city while [[Clone Commander]] [[Cody|CC-2224]] "Cody" was joined by "[[Wooley]]" to investigate the courtyard.<ref name="Innocents" />

Boil and Waxer would encounter a surviving Twi'lek, a girl named [[Numa]], while Cody and Wooley reported in and the rest of the troops moved up and made camp inside a In the wreckage of a larger public building with rows of seating. Having learned that the Twi'leks had been rounded up in the center of town, Kenobi formulated a plan of attack.<ref name="Innocents" />

